{"4928450": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Grand Theft Timeline", "steam_appid": 4928450, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>1-4+ players time-travel kidnapping-collection dungeon-crawling with physics, guns, and a homebase.</strong><br><strong>Operate a makeshift time machine to pull a time travel heist with your friends.</strong><br><strong>Kidnap people across history, steal their treasure, haul them back in cages, and run a time paradox production in your garage.</strong><br><strong>And yes, you can shoot Hitler.</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Pull a time travel heist with your friends. Operate a makeshift time travel machine to traverse the timeline with 200+ buttons, then arrive at a time era, explore it, find the valuable, and steal it (or kidnap it). Just don't get stranded and become part of the timeline yourself. 1-4+ players.</i></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>You and your friends built a time machine - humanity's greatest invention. And you're using it to rob people who haven't invented police yet.</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>It's an online co-op game where you pile into a homemade time machine, with a wall of about four hundred buttons none of you fully understand. Pick a year, and go steal from it. Any year. All of them.</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>The time machine has just about 200 buttons and your friend is pressing all of them to find out what each one does.</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>So you drop into 1503 and lift the Mona Lisa off the wall while it's still just some painting nobody's heard of. You rob a pharaoh's tomb with the mummy still in it. You slip into 2009 and quietly mine a few thousand Bitcoin back when it's worth nothing - the only patient crime four idiots will ever pull off. You steal a dinosaur egg, which goes exactly as well as it sounds, because the mother is the size of a bus and she watched you do it.</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>And it just keeps escalating. You rob the Titanic - and you've got until the iceberg to get out. You clean out a cult in 1990 and take everything they own, which they were going to give away anyway. You jump to the future and steal an actual spaceship. Eventually you stop robbing history and start robbing fiction - yeah, you can go grab the Infinity Stones, and no, the big purple guy is not happy about it.</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>But here's the thing about a time machine: it leaves with whoever's inside it. So when the guards close in and the jump window starts to shut, your best friend is already in the seat - holding all the loot, watching you sprint - deciding whether to hold it and wait. He does not wait. &quot;We left Kevin in 1340. He'll figure it out.&quot;</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Think about it like Lethal Company (Dungeon Crawler / Extraction with Friends) but through many different time eras, each one with its own loot and threats.</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Upgrade your time machine to travel farther in time and better equipment to handle threats better.</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Rob the timeline with your friends. Just don't become part of it yourself.</i><br><br><i>It's a time travel heist. Rob history with your friends. GTT - Grand Theft Timeline.</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>I'll try to release it on the day of GTA 6 release (Grand Theft Auto 6 / Grand Theft Auto VI) if I can finish it in time lol</i></p></li></ul>", "about_the_game": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>1-4+ players time-travel kidnapping-collection dungeon-crawling with physics, guns, and a homebase.</strong><br><strong>Operate a makeshift time machine to pull a time travel heist with your friends.</strong><br><strong>Kidnap people across history, steal their treasure, haul them back in cages, and run a time paradox production in your garage.</strong><br><strong>And yes, you can shoot Hitler.</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Pull a time travel heist with your friends. Operate a makeshift time travel machine to traverse the timeline with 200+ buttons, then arrive at a time era, explore it, find the valuable, and steal it (or kidnap it). Just don't get stranded and become part of the timeline yourself. 1-4+ players.</i></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>You and your friends built a time machine - humanity's greatest invention. And you're using it to rob people who haven't invented police yet.</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>It's an online co-op game where you pile into a homemade time machine, with a wall of about four hundred buttons none of you fully understand. Pick a year, and go steal from it. Any year. All of them.</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>The time machine has just about 200 buttons and your friend is pressing all of them to find out what each one does.</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>So you drop into 1503 and lift the Mona Lisa off the wall while it's still just some painting nobody's heard of. You rob a pharaoh's tomb with the mummy still in it. You slip into 2009 and quietly mine a few thousand Bitcoin back when it's worth nothing - the only patient crime four idiots will ever pull off. You steal a dinosaur egg, which goes exactly as well as it sounds, because the mother is the size of a bus and she watched you do it.</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>And it just keeps escalating. You rob the Titanic - and you've got until the iceberg to get out. You clean out a cult in 1990 and take everything they own, which they were going to give away anyway. You jump to the future and steal an actual spaceship. Eventually you stop robbing history and start robbing fiction - yeah, you can go grab the Infinity Stones, and no, the big purple guy is not happy about it.</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>But here's the thing about a time machine: it leaves with whoever's inside it. So when the guards close in and the jump window starts to shut, your best friend is already in the seat - holding all the loot, watching you sprint - deciding whether to hold it and wait. He does not wait. &quot;We left Kevin in 1340. He'll figure it out.&quot;</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Think about it like Lethal Company (Dungeon Crawler / Extraction with Friends) but through many different time eras, each one with its own loot and threats.</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Upgrade your time machine to travel farther in time and better equipment to handle threats better.</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Rob the timeline with your friends. Just don't become part of it yourself.</i><br><br><i>It's a time travel heist. Rob history with your friends. GTT - Grand Theft Timeline.</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>I'll try to release it on the day of GTA 6 release (Grand Theft Auto 6 / Grand Theft Auto VI) if I can finish it in time lol</i></p></li></ul>", "short_description": "1-4+ players time-travel kidnapping-collection dungeon-crawling with physics, guns, and a homebase. Operate a makeshift time machine to pull a time travel heist with your friends. Kidnap people across history, steal their treasure, haul them back in cages, and run a time paradox production in your garage. And yes, shoot Hitler.", "supported_languages": "English, French, Italian, German, Spanish - Spain, Japanese, Korean, Portuguese - Portugal, Russian, Simplified Chinese, Polish, Turkish", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4928450/e7811867288edcd8a3246f9d74da454e9b9e95c7/header.jpg?t=1787936953", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4928450/3a7055e1eecc328c2a9b1fbb351f1e8d3f1eea44/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1787936953", "capsule_imagev5": "ht